{
  "requirement": "`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its default value is\ncheaply cloneable and claims no extensions. The filename-based constructors\nselect it when no supplied language claims the extension, including filenames\nwithout an extension, under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Structural assessment of `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.language`**\n\nThe obligations are met by the following sources.\n\n- **`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang`.**\n  - The `language!(PlainText, super::plain::PROFILE, \"plain-text-structural-v1\")` invocation in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs` is marked `{impl}`. It expands through `macro[language]` into `impl super::OutlineLang for PlainText`.\n  - That impl supplies `name`, `extensions`, `outline` and `fingerprint_scheme`, and overrides `search_structure`.\n  - `name` and `extensions` read the profile. `outline` delegates to `parse_with(&PROFILE, …)`.\n- **Default value, cheaply cloneable.** The macro declares `PlainText` as a unit struct with `#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]`. Cloning copies nothing, and `Default` exists.\n- **Claims no extensions.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/plain.rs#static[PROFILE]` sets `extensions: &[]`. It has no grammar (`language: None`), so `search_structure` returns `unsupported_search`.\n- **Filename-based constructors select it when no language claims the extension, including filenames without one.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs#impl[OutlineContent]/fn[from_source]` asks `languages::registry().for_path(filename)`. If that returns `None`, it calls `Self::from_source_with(&languages::PlainText, …)`. `from_path` and `from_id` reach it through `from_source`.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/language.rs#impl[Registry]/fn[for_path]` returns `None` for a path without an extension, because `path.extension()?` short-circuits. It lowercases the extension, so matching is case-insensitive.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/profile.rs#fn[profile_for_path]` falls back to `plain::PROFILE`. `sources.rs#fn[parse_snapshot]` also uses `plain::PROFILE` when no provider matches.\n  - `languages::registry()` registers only the eight bundled providers, and none of them claims the plain-text case.\n\nTests exist with `{test}` references to the plain-text declarations: `bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline` asserts the name and empty extensions, and `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors` covers the fallback. I found no structural gap, ambiguity or unmarked-test gap. The nonblank-line outline shape belongs to the refining plain-text declarations, so I didn't assess it here.",
  "references": "d364693a64f673cea5b31c5d57cc4436a3d085824fd398288e275ce0c804733a",
  "inputs": [
